      "priceDate": "2026-11-25",
      "keyPoints": [
        "September quarter: revenue Rs 25.3bn (+19.5% Y/Y, +1.3% Q/Q), EBIT Rs 2.4bn (+32.0%), EBIT margin 9.3% from 8.4%; profit to shareholders Rs 1,513mn (+64.4% Y/Y, +22.7% Q/Q), EPS Rs 2.53.",
        "Hand Protection drove it: operating profit +50.7% Y/Y to Rs 2.0bn, margin 12.0% from 9.9% like-for-like; Plantations' operating profit fell 25.3% to Rs 382mn (margin 4.4% from 6.6%).",
        "A lower tax rate (18.4% vs 35.9%) and lower minority interest lifted earnings, while net finance cost rose to Rs 307mn from Rs 60mn on higher short-term borrowing (Rs 12.7bn vs Rs 8.2bn in March).",
        "1H EBIT of Rs 4.1bn is 54.7% of HSB's FY27E Rs 7.5bn; FY27E EPS kept at Rs 7.29. With the price above the Rs 65 target, the rating is changed to Hold (short-term outlook Neutral).",
        "Valuation: 9.5x trailing P/E (9.8x FY27E) vs a 10-year average of 6.8x and +1 SD of 10.4x; ROE 11.3% vs 16.5% average; 1.2x book (NAV Rs 61.72). Technically overbought (RSI 76) at a 52-week high, first support the 50-day EMA at Rs 61.58."
      ],
      "forecasts": [
        "FY27E revenue Rs 90,963mn",
        "FY27E EBIT Rs 7,519mn, EBITDA Rs 11,037mn",
        "FY27E profit to shareholders Rs 4,360mn, EPS Rs 7.28 (Rs 7.29 in the text)",
        "FY27E effective tax rate 31.0%"
      ],
      "risks": [
        "Receivables up to Rs 22.6bn from Rs 16.4bn, so 1H operating cash flow was only Rs 0.9bn against Rs 4.4bn capex; the gap was borrowed short-term, lifting net debt to Rs 13.5bn from Rs 8.9bn",
        "1H tax rate of 21.8% is well below the 31.0% forecast; a return to it would weigh on 2H",
        "Plantations (1H −17.4%) depends on a seasonally strong 4Q exposed to weather and tea and rubber prices"
      ],
      "catalysts": [
