  "news": [
    {
      "title": "ADB approves $200mn for small businesses",
      "text": "Half is a policy loan to improve the financial system for MSMEs (including a new microfinance regulator, better credit information and guarantees), half a credit line through banks for investment loans, $40mn of it for green loans. MSMEs make up over 52% of GDP and 45% of jobs.",
      "topic": "Economy",
      "figure": "$200mn"
    },
    {
      "title": "Parliament committee wants EV tax breaks",
      "text": "The Committee on Ways and Means called for tax concessions to make electric vehicles affordable and for rules to manage used EV batteries; it also discussed vehicle import taxes and Customs clearance delays.",
      "topic": "Policy"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inflation rises to 8.5% in October",
      "text": "NCPI inflation rose to 8.5% from 8.1% (2.7% a year earlier): food 7.2%, non-food 9.5%, with transport (petrol) the biggest contributor. The central bank raised its policy rate 25 bps to 9% last week and the reserve ratio to 3% from 9 December, expects CCPI inflation near 9% in November and back to 5% only in the second half of 2027.",
      "topic": "Economy",
      "figure": "8.5%"
    },
    {
      "title": "IMF board to consider seventh review on 2 Dec",
      "text": "Approval would release about $345mn, bringing disbursements under the $3bn facility to about $2.7bn; the meeting also covers waivers and changes to performance criteria.",
      "topic": "Economy",
      "figure": "$345mn"
    },
    {
      "title": "Remittances heading for a record $9bn",
      "text": "The Foreign Minister said $7.6bn had arrived by end-October and about $1.5bn more is expected in November–December, against $8.1bn last year. Overseas missions earned Rs 6.6bn from consular services.",
      "topic": "Economy",
      "figure": "$9bn"
    },
    {
      "title": "Cabinet approves $30mn OPEC Fund loan",
      "text": "A policy-based loan ($24mn ordinary and $6mn special resources) to support the reform programme alongside the World Bank's development policy operation.",
      "topic": "Economy",
      "figure": "$30mn"
    },
    {
      "title": "US futures slip after tech sell-off; Asia falls",
      "text": "On Tuesday the S&P 500 fell 0.5% and the Nasdaq 1.5% as Nvidia fell, while the Dow rose 0.9%; futures were slightly lower ahead of inflation data. Kospi fell about 4.5% at Wednesday's open and Nikkei 1.4%.",
      "topic": "Global markets",
      "figure": "−1.5%"
    },
    {
      "title": "Oil at a three-month low",
      "text": "Brent fell 3.46% to $89.37 and WTI 3.88% to $80.17 on Monday as Middle East supply rose and Libya's Sharara pipeline restarted; JPMorgan sees the high $70s in the first half of 2027 on a supply surplus.",
      "topic": "Energy",
      "figure": "$89.37"
    }
  ],
